### Runtime Query
```gdscript
var registry = GameBridge.get_bridge_methods()
# registry = {
#   "methods": [
#     {"name": "spawn_entity", "owner": "EntityManager"},
#     {"name": "set_linear_velocity", "owner": "PhysicsController"},
#     ...
#   ],
#   "byModule": {
#     "EntityManager": ["spawn_entity", "destroy_entity", ...],
#     "PhysicsController": ["set_linear_velocity", ...],
#     ...
#   },
#   "total": 87
# }
```

### Collision Detection (if duplicate found)
```
WARNING: [GameBridge][REGISTRY] COLLISION: Method 'spawn_entity' registered multiple times
```

## Production Behavior
- No startup logs (respects `OS.is_debug_build()`)
- Runtime query still available via `get_bridge_methods()`
- No collision warnings

## Verification
- [x] Startup summary logs in dev mode
- [x] Runtime query returns method registry
- [x] Methods grouped by owner module
- [x] Collision detection warns on duplicates
- [x] Production mode suppresses logs
- [x] Evidence file created

## Notes
- Method ownership classification is heuristic-based (naming patterns)
- Future refactor could use explicit module registration
- Collision detection currently only warns (doesn't prevent registration)
- Runtime query can be called from JS bridge or GDScript
